  </header>
  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">APEX RELAY JOURNAL</p>
      <h1>Notes from the paddock</h1>
      <p class="lede">Practice drills and race briefing notes for drivers who run their own sim racing lobbies. The photographs illustrate each scenario.</p>
      <nav class="story-toc" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#apex">Following at race pace</a><a href="#pit">The driver swap</a><a href="#cockpit">Build a repeatable rig</a></nav>
    </header>
    <article class="media-story" id="apex">
      <figure class="story-figure">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/apex/media/apex-480.webp 480w, /assets/apex/media/apex-800.webp 800w, /assets/apex/media/apex-1280.webp 1280w" sizes="(max-width: 690px) calc(100vw - 32px), (max-width: 900px) calc((100vw - 80px) * .6), (max-width: 1416px) calc((100vw - 136px) * .6), 768px">
            <img src="/assets/apex/media/apex-800.jpg" width="800" height="533" alt="Two touring cars follow a fast road circuit curve past the painted kerb" fetchpriority="high">
          </picture>
        <figcaption>Practice scenario with two cars on the same line through a fast curve.</figcaption>
        <a class="original" href="/assets/apex/media/apex-original.jpg" download aria-label="Download the practice session, full resolution JPEG, 650 KB">Full resolution JPEG · 650 KB</a>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Open practice</p>
        <h2>Following at race pace</h2>
        <p>Run a repeatable traffic drill before your first sprint.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Baseline</dt>
          <dd>Give each driver a clear lap on the same fuel load. Pick a braking marker and a reference gap before pairing up.</dd>
          <dt>Follow</dt>
          <dd>Keep the same reference gap for three laps. Start braking early enough to keep the same gap on entry. Use the replay to see where the two lines diverge.</dd>
          <dt>Swap</dt>
          <dd>Switch the leader and repeat. Compare one corner at a time and agree on an approach before reducing the gap.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="media-story" id="pit">
      <figure class="story-figure">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/apex/media/pit-480.webp 480w, /assets/apex/media/pit-800.webp 800w, /assets/apex/media/pit-1280.webp 1280w" sizes="(max-width: 690px) calc(100vw - 32px), (max-width: 900px) calc((100vw - 80px) * .6), (max-width: 1416px) calc((100vw - 136px) * .6), 768px">
            <img src="/assets/apex/media/pit-800.jpg" width="800" height="533" alt="A GT car sits beside an illuminated garage in an endurance pit lane at dusk" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </picture>
        <figcaption>Endurance pit scenario with a lit garage ahead of a stationary GT car.</figcaption>
        <a class="original" href="/assets/apex/media/pit-original.jpg" download aria-label="Download the driver swap, full resolution JPEG, 911 KB">Full resolution JPEG · 911 KB</a>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Team endurance</p>
        <h2>The driver swap</h2>
        <p>Make the changeover routine boring before race day.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Before the lap</dt>
          <dd>Confirm fuel, tyres and the next driver in voice chat. Agree on who calls the pit entry and who confirms the changeover.</dd>
          <dt>At the line</dt>
          <dd>Practise engaging the limiter before the line and stopping on the marker. Do a dry run of the simulator’s swap procedure before adding a tyre change.</dd>
          <dt>At pit exit</dt>
          <dd>Read the relative timing and mirror before merging. Treat the first lap after the swap as a reference lap to check the new driver’s controls.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="media-story" id="cockpit">
      <figure class="story-figure">
          <picture>
            <source type="image/webp" srcset="/assets/apex/media/cockpit-480.webp 480w, /assets/apex/media/cockpit-800.webp 800w, /assets/apex/media/cockpit-1280.webp 1280w" sizes="(max-width: 690px) calc(100vw - 32px), (max-width: 900px) calc((100vw - 80px) * .6), (max-width: 1416px) calc((100vw - 136px) * .6), 768px">
            <img src="/assets/apex/media/cockpit-800.jpg" width="800" height="533" alt="A driver sits at a sim racing wheel facing a curved circuit display" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </picture>
        <figcaption>Sim racing cockpit with a curved screen and a simple wheel layout.</figcaption>
        <a class="original" href="/assets/apex/media/cockpit-original.jpg" download aria-label="Download the sim racing cockpit, full resolution JPEG, 527 KB">Full resolution JPEG · 527 KB</a>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Driver setup</p>
        <h2>Build a repeatable rig</h2>
        <p>Set up the wheel, pedals and field of view before changing the car.</p>
        <dl>
          <dt>Calibrate</dt>
          <dd>Place the seat so you can apply full brake pressure while staying supported. Set the input range and verify that the pedals return to zero.</dd>
          <dt>Check sightlines</dt>
          <dd>Set the field of view based on the screen size and distance. Check that you can see the apex and the essential timing information without leaning.</dd>
          <dt>Save a baseline</dt>
          <dd>Write down the seating position, steering range and pedal settings. Save a copy in the simulator so a new profile is easy to compare.</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <footer class="wrap footer">
    <strong>Apex Relay</strong>
    <nav aria-label="Footer"><a href="/privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="/terms.html">Site terms</a></nav>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
EOF_PADDOCK_HTML
