<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="description" content="Compare a transfer with its restoration and estimate a cassette or reel project.">
<link rel="icon" href="/assets/archive/favicon.png" type="image/png">
<title>Archive help · Signal Archive</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/archive/site.css?v=e11c3659ae">
</head>
<body class="archive">
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
<header class="wrap mast"><a class="brand" href="/"><span aria-hidden="true">◉</span>Signal Archive</a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/index.html">Home</a><a href="/studio.html">Listen & estimate</a><a href="/formats.html">Formats</a><a href="/cases.html">Case library</a><a href="/delivery.html">Delivery</a></nav></header>
<main class="wrap" id="main">
<header class="intro"><p class="tag">Transfer help</p><h1>Common questions</h1><p class="lede">Questions that affect the estimate, original transfer and set of files you keep.</p></header><section class="panel"><details><summary>How do different formats share an estimate?</summary><p class="spaced">Add one transfer line per group of items with the same recorded minutes, format and restoration option.</p></details><details><summary>Can I keep both versions?</summary><p class="spaced">Yes. Plan for both WAV copies in the archive calculator when you want both versions lossless.</p></details><details><summary>What if the listed length is only approximate?</summary><p class="spaced">Start from the label and record assumptions beside the estimate. Billed minutes depend on the recorded material transferred.</p></details><details><summary>How is the comparison timed?</summary><p class="spaced">Each demonstration pair is the same duration. Switching versions carries the player time into the selected track.</p></details><details><summary>Which sample should I use?</summary><p class="spaced">Choose by the main issue you hear. Pitch drift, impulses, dropouts and steady noise call for different listening checks.</p></details><p class="spaced"><a href="/planning.html">Estimate archive size</a> · <a href="/cases.html">Listen to restoration cases</a></p></section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap footer"><strong>Signal Archive</strong><a href="/formats.html">Formats</a></footer>
</body>
</html>
EOF_ARCHIVE_HELP_HTML
