<header class="intro"><p class="tag">Cassette</p><h1>A damaged rehearsal tape</h1><p class="lede">Level dropouts · 16 second listening sample</p></header><section class="labgrid"><article class="panel"><div class="panel-head"><p class="tag">Listening room</p><h2>Before and after</h2></div><p>The transfer dips in level around 0:03, 0:06, 0:08, 0:10 and 0:13. Use the comparison to hear the effect of a continuous signal.</p><div class="toggle" role="group" aria-label="Recording version"><button type="button" data-audio="before" aria-pressed="true">Before · transfer</button><button type="button" data-audio="after" aria-pressed="false">After · restored</button></div><audio id="sample" controls preload="none" data-base="/assets/archive/samples/practice-" src="/assets/archive/samples/practice-before.mp3" aria-label="Audio restoration comparison"></audio><p class="micro" id="player-status" role="status">Selected: before, raw transfer.</p><p class="micro">Synthetic demonstration · 16 seconds</p></article><article class="panel"><h2>Restoration notes</h2><dl class="steps"><dt>Assess</dt><dd>Log the dropouts with approximate timestamps and check whether they recur on a second playback.</dd><dt>Treat</dt><dd>Compare any alternate transfer before making repairs. In this synthetic example the intact signal demonstrates the target.</dd><dt>Deliver</dt><dd>Document repaired sections and retain the original transfer alongside the listening master.</dd></dl></article></section><section class="section"><h2>Estimate a similar transfer</h2><p class="spaced">The estimate starts with one 60 minute item and restoration. Adjust those values for your recording.</p><p class="spaced"><a class="button" href="/estimate.html?format=cassette&minutes=60&restore=1#estimate">Use this example in the estimate</a></p><p class="spaced"><a href="/cases.html">Browse other cases</a> · <a href="/delivery.html">See delivery formats</a></p></section>
</main>
<footer class="wrap footer"><strong>Signal Archive</strong><a href="/formats.html">Formats</a></footer>
</body>
</html>
EOF_CASES_PRACTICE_HTML
