<main class="wrap" id="main">
<header class="intro"><p class="tag">Compact cassette</p><h1>Shell, sides and levels</h1><p class="lede">Write down the tape type and track order before timing the project.</p></header><article class="panel"><h2>What to note before transfer</h2><dl class="steps"><dt>Sides and order</dt><dd>Label sides A and B and note if the same material appears on both. The listed minutes should include only the sides you want transferred.</dd><dt>Noise reduction</dt><dd>Record any Dolby mark on the cassette or cover and keep that note with the transfer instructions.</dd><dt>Condition</dt><dd>A loose pressure pad, creased tape or damaged shell changes the handling required. Keep the recording in its case.</dd></dl><p class="spaced"><a href="/cases/hiss.html">Cassette listening copy</a> · <a href="/formats.html">All formats and rates</a></p></article>
</main>
<footer class="wrap footer"><strong>Signal Archive</strong><a href="/formats.html">Formats</a></footer>
</body>
