<main class="wrap" id="main">
<header class="intro"><p class="tag">Microcassette</p><h1>Recorder speed and quiet passages</h1><p class="lede">Identify the recorder when possible and note the sides that contain material.</p></header><article class="panel"><h2>What to note before transfer</h2><dl class="steps"><dt>Source recorder</dt><dd>Use the notes on the shell or recorder to check whether the material uses 1.2 or 2.4 cm/s.</dd><dt>Quiet sections</dt><dd>Check the listening copy between speech or notes. A faint occupied passage can sound like a silent gap on a small speaker.</dd><dt>Mark interruptions</dt><dd>Flag pauses, repeats and unexpected interruptions if they matter to the sequence.</dd></dl><p class="spaced"><a href="/cases/pocket.html">Pocket recorder example</a> · <a href="/formats.html">All formats and rates</a></p></article>
