<main class="wrap" id="main">
<header class="intro"><p class="tag">Open reel ¼″</p><h1>Speed and track layout</h1><p class="lede">Reel diameter helps describe the item. The recorded speed and track layout determine playback.</p></header><article class="panel"><h2>What to note before transfer</h2><dl class="steps"><dt>Playback speed</dt><dd>Check the box for inches per second or a duration note. Common label markings include 3¾ and 7½ ips.</dd><dt>Track layout</dt><dd>Note mono, stereo or multiple tracks when marked. A reel can hold more than one tracking arrangement.</dd><dt>Leader and winding</dt><dd>Keep the source in its own box and record which end is presented if the label specifies tails out.</dd></dl><p class="spaced"><a href="/cases/reel.html">Open reel pitch example</a> · <a href="/formats.html">All formats and rates</a></p></article>
</main>
<footer class="wrap footer"><strong>Signal Archive</strong><a href="/formats.html">Formats</a></footer>
