<main class="wrap" id="main">
<section class="hero"><div><p class="tag">Analog audio transfer</p><h1>Old recordings.<br>Clearer sound.</h1><p class="lede">Digitize cassettes and open reel recordings, then hear what careful cleanup changes.</p><a class="button" href="/studio.html">Hear the difference</a></div><figure><img src="/assets/archive/tape.webp" srcset="/assets/archive/tape-640.webp 640w, /assets/archive/tape.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 780px) calc(100vw - 32px), (max-width: 1280px) calc((100vw - 112px) * .55), 642px" width="1200" height="800" alt="Open reel tape deck on an audio archive workbench" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>The transfer bench</figcaption></figure></section><section class="section"><h2>From original to listening copy</h2><div class="tiles"><article><h3>Listen</h3><p>Switch between the transfer and restoration during the same playback. The sample makes noise and level differences easy to hear.</p></article><article><h3>Estimate</h3><p>Price by recording format, item count and recorded minutes. Add restoration per recorded minute.</p></article><article><h3>Deliver</h3><p>A preservation master keeps the captured signal. A separate listening copy carries the cleanup you choose.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><h2>Find a comparable recording</h2><div class="tiles"><article class="catalog-card" data-category="cassette"><p class="tag">Cassette</p><h2><a href="/cases/hiss.html">Cassette listening copy</a></h2><p>Broadband hiss and hum</p></article>
